※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=7 diag=none

※ A function whose header has no arrow answers with nothing.  There is no name
※ to write for that: writing one out would be a second way of saying what the
※ absence already says.

let counter: mut u6 = 0u6

@[constructor, impure]
fn prepare():
    counter ← 7u6

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    counter
